Using {lado} is asking for trouble.  I couldn't find proof that the grammar
forbids it, but consider what would happen if the following word hadn't
begun with a vowel.  How would you tell "lado mark." from "la domark."?  I
suppose "lado .mark." would require a pause before the name.  I'd use la
.egeriam. ne do or something.
